fect but having an idea of where  things are going will really help  because if you can't say here's how I'm  gonna spend this money you're giving me  nobody's gonna give you the money to  find your dream  [Music]  number four is understanding trends and  understanding do the trend support where  you're going or not you know if your  business is around self-driving cars  that's gonna happen it may not happen  right now may not happen in the next two  years but like five six ten years down  the road it's going to happen so that is  a trend that is really supporting you if  you need people to be driving in their  cars for your business to be a success  that's not a trend that's really  supporting you and so understanding  where trends are going and understanding  the realistic timeline for that  happening you want to focus on that and  have a clear understanding and put that  into your plan number five is  understanding technology is the  technology currently in place for you to  be able to do what you want to do or do  you need improvements in technology to  happen this is one of the things that  investors always look at in the business  plan if the technology is ready right  now there's an audience the tech is  right there you don't need some new  things to happen they're much more  likely to fund you then if you need to  wait for the cost of some technology to  come down if you go out and acquire it  so if we look at driverless cars as an  example the tech isn't there yet but  it's not quite ready for you yet so if  you're planning the big mission around  it you need to wait a little bit right  you can lay the groundwork you can get  it all started but for you to really hit  at home if you need people to have this  as an adopted technology we're not there  yet and so having that as part of your  plan looking at the estimations look at  the growth curve to understand how far  away that is you want to plan that in if  the tech is already ready you don't need  any cos